* Fri Oct 09 2026 nicolataibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com> - 2026.10.09.03
  - GDD contract (layout): the CPU/GPU boundary contract is now pinned
    FIELD BY FIELD, not just by size. include/spacegl_gdd.h gains the
    full set of compile-time _Static_asserts — every field offset of
    GddVertex (pos@0, color@16, normal@32, mode@44, local@48,
    metallic@64, roughness@68), of GddInstance, GddPC, GddCounts and
    GddScenePC, plus the GLSL alignment rule itself (every vec4 start
    of GddVertex on a 16-byte boundary) — and gdd_contract_test
    re-checks the same set at runtime (test_layout extended from 3 to
    48 checks: sizes, per-field offsets, alignment), so a mis-compiled
    TU or a different-compiler layout cannot sneak through. gdd_contract
    passes with 362 checks (was 317).
  - Vulkan (validation layers): Debug builds (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug,
    i.e. NDEBUG not defined) now request the standard
    VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation layer BY DEFAULT in createInstance():
    sync/barrier and pipeline errors are reported by the driver at the
    moment they happen instead of surfacing later as silent GPU
    corruption (the class that cost a manual hunt in the additive
    funnel). Release builds are unchanged (no layers by default). The
    new SPACEGL_VALIDATION variable overrides the build default (=0
    off, =1 on — e.g. to audit a Release binary); the standard
    VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS variable is honored as before and merged with
    the default (a layer the driver lacks is warned and skipped).
  - Shader (gdd_scene.frag): microguard on the PBR specular term —
    vRough is clamped to [0, 1] before pow(dot(N,H), 32*(1-rough)):
    if the GPU ever carried roughness > 1 the exponent went negative
    and pow(0.0, neg) (a zero N-H dot) evaluates to inf/NaN in GLSL.
    The builder always writes [0, 1]; the guard makes the shader total
    anyway. Also dropped the stray "[cite: 17]" tooling markers and the
    ragged comment indentation of gdd_scene.vert, and fixed the GddPC
    _Static_assert message that said 32 B for the 36-B struct.
