    first usable entry wins: 1) the official VULKAN_SDK environment
    variable - the explicit per-machine override: set and usable it
    wins over everything, set but unusable it WARNS and the chain
    continues, so a stale export cannot brick the build; 2) the pinned
    default SDK - the documented project decision
    (/home/nick/dev/c/vulkan-sdk/1.4.363.0/x86_64) for reproducible
    builds with headers, loader and glslc from the same SDK; the
    USE_DEFAULT_VULKAN_SDK / DEFAULT_VULKAN_SDK cache knobs are
    preserved, the opt-out still works; 3) the system Vulkan -
    find_package(Vulkan) (official config, else CMake's FindVulkan
    module: libvulkan + system headers), then, as last resort, the
    distro from-source loader package (VulkanLoader, the Vulkan::Loader
    target + the distro vulkan/vulkan.h). That last step is what
    actually exists on Fedora: there is no VulkanConfig.cmake, so the
    pre-fix fallback `find_package(Vulkan REQUIRED)` could not have
    succeeded on this machine (the build only ever worked because the
