  - Server (command grammar): added "vec <H> <M> <S>" (handle_vec in
    src/server/commands.c), the vector-thrust command the pilot
    hat-switch needed: it sets the flight vector from the requested
    course and cruises NAV_STATE_IMPULSE along it WITHOUT touching the
    attitude — van_h/van_m/van_r stay exactly as they are, so the ship
    translates (brake / lateral / vertical) while the cockpit view
    stays on the current nose. "vec <H> <M> 0" releases the thrust
    (IDLE, flight vector zeroed, "Vector thrust released. All stop.",
    same stop semantics as the 1-arg impulse); the speed clamps to
    SPEED_IMPULSE_TICK_MAX, the course folds through normalize_upright,
    the cost is COST_ACTION_HIGH with the same impulse-system-critical
    and energy guards as handle_imp; the command is registered in
    command_registry ("help" lists it) and in the docked auto-undock
    movement set (nav/imp/pos/jum/und + vec, so a docked ship undocks
    on vector thrust like on any other movement command). The pre-fix
    hat could not work without a grammar change: the 3-arg impulse
    ALWAYS aligns the nose to the target course (NAV_STATE_ALIGN_
    IMPULSE, up to a 1 s ramp), so "imp (h0+180) -m0 S" rolled the ship
    180 deg — the cockpit view spun for a whole second — before any
    burn, and in NO hat position did a thruster ever read as firing
    (the 2026.10.07.01 latch had fixed the target source, not the
    command's align-then-burn nature).
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the hat switch now fires a VECTORED retro-thruster
    for every one of its 8 directions (pilot_hat_retro →
    pilot_send_vec, src/spacegl_vulkan.c): on the rising edge the
    ship's live course is captured ONCE and the retro vector built
    from it — H* = (h0 + 180) % 360, M* = -m0, the exact reverse of
    the nose — with the per-position strengths UP 10 / RIGHT 40 /
    LEFT 80 / DOWN 100 % and the diagonal +/-15 deg mark drift (the
    2026.10.06.05 8-way layout, now real: each position is a distinct
    thruster firing in its own direction while the view stays put). The
    command fires IMMEDIATELY on the edge (force-bypass of the 10 Hz
    gate), is re-asserted while the hat stays off-center (pilot_
    send_vec's change-detection keeps it to one wire command per
    actuation) with the throttle and stick branches suppressed for the
    whole hold (the brake wins against the throttle); when the hat
    returns to center a latched "vec H* M* 0" releases the thrust, so
    the retro-impulse no longer outlives the hat. No view cycling is
    bound to the hat (the manual "pilot" toggle is unchanged).
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the stick is now a CLOSED-LOOP rate controller on
    the ship's LIVE course (SHM, 60 Hz): the 3-arg "imp" targets
    (live_h - ax * JS_YAW_AHEAD, live_m + ay * JS_PITCH_AHEAD), and the
    server's 1 s alignment ramp turns the ship at (lead x deflection)
    deg/s — JS_YAW_AHEAD 90, JS_PITCH_AHEAD 60 — continuously while
    held, settling onto the last target on release. YAW SENSE FIXED:
    right stick (ax > 0) now turns the nose RIGHT — the target heading
    is BELOW the live one (the pre-fix pilotHeading += ax * JS_YAW_RATE
    sent the nose left); pitch keeps forward = down (mark > 0,
    2026.10.07.01). The speed is max(throttle, stick), so full stick
    still moves the ship at 100 % even at throttle rest (2026.10.07.01's
    vectored-thrust requirement, now honest). The pre-fix open-loop
    accumulation (3.5 deg/frame yaw) ran far ahead of the real ship:
    every ramp sawtoothed behind the runaway target (the stuttering
    "pauses" in the middle of maneuvers), the dedup swallowed the
    commands the ship had already overshot, and the twist "pos" rolled
    a stale local pilotRoll — all three are now live-referenced (the
