* Tue Oct 06 2026 nicolataibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com> - 2026.10.06.07
  - Client: fixed the SIGSEGV on Ctrl+C / SIGTERM / exit (the 2026-10-06
    pilot session core, pid 39068: kernel "spacegl_client[39090]: segfault
    ... error 6" — a WRITE fault on a not-present page by the
    network-listener thread while the main thread sat in the exit-handler
    chain at _fini). Root cause: handle_sigint() called exit() from the
    signal context, so atexit cleanup() ran kill + munmap of the SHM while
    the listener thread was still alive (g_running was never cleared) and
    kept writing g_shared_state on every 60 Hz PKT_UPDATE — a
    use-after-munmap. handle_sigint now only sets g_running (async-signal
    safe; the handler has no SA_RESTART, so the main loop's blocking
    read(STDIN) returns EINTR and the loop exits); the post-loop shutdown
    releases the terminal, JOINS the listener (new g_listener_thread /
    g_listener_started globals) and only then cleanup() (now idempotent
    and NULLing g_shm/g_shared_state before the munmap) tears the SHM
    down. The listener's own teardown paths (server close, read error,
    malloc failure) no longer call exit() from the thread: they set
    g_running and break, and main() owns the process exit; the "xxx" /
    "exit" / "quit" command path breaks to the same shutdown instead of
    exit(0). read_all() now retries on EINTR (pre-fix a Ctrl+C in the
    main thread surfaced in the listener as -1 and was misread as a dead
    connection).
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the right-thumb trigger now sends "pha <E>" with
    PILOT_PHA_ENERGY = 250 — the one-argument form of handle_pha, which
    resolves the currently locked target and answers "No target locked."
    when none is held. The pre-fix bare "pha" (zero args) fell into the
    server's args != 1 && != 2 branch and was ALWAYS rejected with
    "Usage: pha <ID> <E>." (the repeated lines in the 2026-10-06 log): the
    beam phasers had never fired from the stick.
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the "imp" uplink is now rate-limited AND change-
    detected (new pilot_send_imp, jsLastImpH/M/S sentinels on VulkanApp,
    reset on entering pilot mode and in initVulkan): a command is re-sent
    only when the rounded course/speed actually changes (same rounding as
    the wire format, H/M to 0.1 deg, S to 0.001; h=360.0 is safe — the
    server's normalize_upright folds it to 0 via fmod). The pre-fix code
    re-sent the identical "imp" at 10 Hz while the stick sat still and the
    server answered "Course plotted. Aligning for Impulse drive." for every
    duplicate — the spam that drowned the command deck in the log. The ALL
    STOP button syncs the sentinels with its direct "imp 0 0 0" send so a
    re-engagement at the same rounded values is not swallowed by the dedup.
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the hat-switch retro-thruster is now LATCHED
    (pilot_hat_retro): while the hat stays off-center the retro impulse
    (imp H+180 -M speed, per-position strengths UP 10 / RIGHT 40 / LEFT 80
    / DOWN 100 %, diagonals +/-15 deg mark, H/M from the live SHM course) is
    re-asserted on the imp cadence and the throttle impulse is suppressed,
    so the brake actually slows the ship. The pre-fix one-shot fire on the
    hat edge was overwritten by the next throttle "imp" before it could
    bite — with any throttle above the dead zone the ship never braked.
  - Pilot (Vulkan): the "remove after debug" DIAG prints (JS poll once per
    second, show_bridge transitions, every queued command) are now gated
    behind SPACEGL_PILOT_DIAG=1 (pilot_diag_on / PILOT_DIAG) and silent by
    default.
  - IPC command queue: both producers now copy into the 128-byte slot with
    a bounded, NUL-terminated memcpy (vulkan_send_ipc_command in
    src/spacegl_vulkan.c and send_ipc_command in src/spacegl_3dview.c).
    The 3dview variant was strncpy(..., 127) with no explicit terminator —
    a source of 127+ chars left the slot unterminated and the client's
    drain (strncpy into PacketCommand.cmd) could over-read into the next
    slot; the bounded copy also silences -Wstringop-truncation in the
    Vulkan build.

