* Wed Sep 30 2026 nicolataibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com> - 2026.09.30.01
  - spacegl_vulkan: follow-up to the 2026.09.29.05 resize fix — the
    CPU-driven path rendered nothing and the frame pacing was not
    spec-clean; both audited with the Khronos validation layer
    (VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation) on Intel Arc.
    (1) CPU-driven black screen: the resize fix moved the five CPU
    pipelines to dynamic viewport/scissor with viewportCount/
    scissorCount = 0, which is only legal with the
    VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_*_WITH_COUNT variants
    (VUID-...-viewportCount-04135 / scissorCount-04136); with classic
    dynamic state the counts stay 1 and only the VALUES are updated
    per frame (vkCmdSetViewport/vkCmdSetScissor in recordCommandBuffer)
    — the initial pipeline values are placeholders, exactly like the
    GDD scene pipeline that already worked. (2) In-flight fence:
    vkQueuePresentKHR takes no fence, and the old fence-on-render-
    submit signaled while the present operation was still consuming
    the slot's renderFinished semaphore and swapchain image, so the
    3-frame-later reuse re-signaled it mid-use (VUID-vkQueueSubmit-
    pSignalSemaphores-00067); the fence now rides an empty submit
    issued AFTER the present (queue ops run in order, so it signals
    only once the present is done) — on BOTH the CPU drawFrame and
    the GDD gdd_draw_frame. (3) CPU drawFrame early-exit (acquire
    timeout/failure) now resets the slot fence and re-signals it with
    an empty submit: before, that path left the fence unsignaled and
    the next use of the slot waited in vkWaitForFences forever — a
    hard deadlock of the whole loop (GDD already had this); the reset
    is required because vkQueueSubmit wants an unsignaled fence. (4)
    VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR on PRESENT (a present can race the resize
    callback) now triggers recreateSwapChain() on both paths. (5)
    The command pool is created with
    VK_COMMAND_POOL_CREATE_RESET_COMMAND_BUFFER_BIT: the command
    buffers are re-recorded every frame (VUID-vkResetCommandBuffer-
    commandBuffer-00046, hit every frame). (6) cleanup() starts with
    vkDeviceWaitIdle, draining pending submits AND presents before
    freeing the GDD command buffers, destroying the pool, the
    semaphores and the fences (VUID-vkDestroyCommandPool-commandPool-
    00041, vkDestroyFence-fence-01120, vkDestroySemaphore-
    semaphore-05149). (7) The swapchain minImageCount now respects
    VkSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR (this driver reports 3; the hardcoded 2
    violated VUID-VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR-presentMode-02839). (8)
    sampleShadingEnable is now VK_FALSE: the sampleRateShading device
    feature is not enabled and the shaders do not use SRA (VUID-
    VkPipelineMultisampleStateCreateInfo-sampleShadingEnable-00784).
    All the VUIDs above are the ones the layer reported in a pre-fix
    run. Post-fix smoke test: the CPU-driven and the GDD
    (SPACEGL_GPD=1) paths both render, resize cleanly and exit
    through cleanup().

