* Tue Sep 29 2026 nicolataibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com> - 2026.09.29.05
  - spacegl_vulkan: resizing the window no longer freezes the display.
    createSwapChain() hardcoded the extent to {1920,1080}
    (WIDTH/HEIGHT) and no glfwSetFramebufferSizeCallback existed, so
    after any resize vkAcquireNextImageKHR started returning
    VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR, drawFrame()/gdd_draw_frame() early-
    returned on every frame and the window stayed black and frozen
    until exit (handling VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR alone is not enough: an
    extent mismatch is exactly the OUT_OF_DATE case). Fix, keeping
    the window resizable: (1) the extent now follows the live window
    size, clamped to VkSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR (pickSwapChainExtent);
    (2) a new glfwSetFramebufferSizeCallback triggers
    recreateSwapChain(), which rebuilds only the extent-dependent
    resources — swapchain, its image views, the MSAA color/depth
    attachments, the framebuffers, and the GDD MSAA attachments via
    the new gdd_recreate_size_dependent() — while the pipelines
    survive as-is, because viewport/scissor became dynamic on the
    five CPU pipelines (set per frame from the live extent in
    recordCommandBuffer) and the projection aspect now reads
    app->swapChainExtent instead of WIDTH/HEIGHT; (3) as a backstop,
    VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR on acquire (both the CPU drawFrame and
    the GDD gdd_draw_frame, which re-signals its slot fence with an
    empty submit to keep the triple-buffer invariant) now triggers
    recreateSwapChain() and skips the frame, so the loop self-heals
    even if the resize callback is missed.

